commit.message:
fix(pathkernel): make each stage type valid by construction

Review of PR #4123, findings 1 to 6, one rule for each class:
- valid by construction: private fields, checked constructors, and
  validated newtypes in each enum variant (WorkPlane, ToolShape, Hop,
  GuideChoice, LoadControl, Proof, Verdict::Incomplete);
- order: a curve may only be restarted (closed) or reversed, with its
  circle; the start is the first point of the first curve;
- plan: the step law is a transition table; a cut consumes readiness;
- entry: each proof names its place; the descent stays in it;
- load: the limit domain, valid records, each reading over the limit
  named once, each record agrees with a reading;
- guide: a total order of the set, with a geometric tie-break.

The tests use the public API in the new suite tests/laws.rs.

Refs #4055

